(a) whether the Rare Earth Corridor announced for Andhra Pradesh in the Union Budget 2026-27 has formally been notified;
(b) if not, the reasons for the delay and the expected timeline for its notification;
(c) the current status of rollout of Rare Earth Permanent Magnet (REPM) scheme; and
(d) the steps being taken to ensure timely operationalisation of the Corridor to support the State’s monazite-based rare earth processing ecosystem?

(a) the current status of development of National Waterway-4 (Godavari-Krishna), including the stretch between Vijayawada and Muktyala in Andhra Pradesh, along with details of works undertaken such as Ro-Ro terminals;
(b) the funds allocated and released to Andhra Pradesh for development of National Waterways during each of the last three years;
(c) the details of cargo/passenger movement, if any, presently operational on National Waterway-4 within the State; and
(d) the challenges, if any, such as seasonal flow variation or land acquisition, affecting the pace of waterway development in the State?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any survey/study regarding medical tourism for AYUSH in the country over the last five years;
(b) if so, the details regarding the steps undertaken to boost medical tourism in AYUSH sector across the country over the last five years, especially in Andhra Pradesh;
(c) the details regarding total amount of funds allocated, released and utilised over the last five years for the purposes of boosting medical tourism in AYUSH Sector across the country, State-wise including Andhra Pradesh; and
(d) whether Government has undertaken any program to raise awareness of AYUSH Sector amongst foreign countries, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether the Dumpsite Remediation Accelerator Programme (DRAP) has been launched across the country;
(b) if so, the details of sites taken up and completed, along with funds allocated and released for each site and the criteria adopted for prioritising such sites, year-wise;
(c) whether any long-term monitoring mechanism has been put in place after remediation, if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether Government has assessed the environmental and public health benefits achieved through the remediation works, if so, the details and outcomes thereof; and
(e) whether there are any plans to expand or accelerate the programme, if so, the details thereof, if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government provides credit support to farmers for creation or acquisition of long-term agricultural assets, including farm machinery, irrigation structures, post-harvest infrastructure, etc;
(b) if so, the details of number of beneficiaries supported during the last three years under such schemes, year-wise, State-wise and district-wise for Andhra Pradesh;
(c) the quantum of credit disbursed for long-term agricultural assets under various Government-supported credit schemes, during the last three years, year-wise, State-wise; and
(d) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of gaps or constraints faced by farmers in building long term agriculture infrastructure, particularly small, marginal and tenant farmers?

(a) the tourism potential and key attractions of Andhra Pradesh identified by the Ministry, including its coastline, heritage and pilgrimage circuits;
(b) the status of Central assistance extended to Andhra Pradesh under schemes such as Swadesh Darshan and PRASHAD for development of tourism circuits in the State;
(c) whether Government proposes to identify and develop new tourism circuits in Andhra Pradesh covering its coastal, heritage and eco-tourism destinations; and
(d) the details of Central assistance extended to Andhra Pradesh for tourism infrastructure development during the last three years?

(a) the current status of implementation of the National Animal Disease Control Programme (NADCP) in Andhra Pradesh, and the progress achieved in controlling Foot and Mouth Disease and Brucellosis in the State;
(b) the adequacy of veterinary hospitals, dispensaries, cold-chain infrastructure, and trained vaccinators/disease surveillance personnel presently available in the State under the Programme;
(c) the key implementation challenges, if any, being faced by Andhra Pradesh in achieving effective disease control coverage; and
(d) whether any proposal for extension of the Programme or its next phase is under consideration, and if so, the details thereof?

