(a) the status and timeline of finalisation and notification of the draft Floating Solar PV (FSPV) Potential Assessment Report and the draft Floating Solar Policy prepared by the National Institute of Solar Energy (NISE) and IIT Roorkee;
(b) the total floating solar potential identified across water bodies in the country under this assessment, State/UT-wise;
(c) whether the draft policy proposes a single-window clearance mechanism for floating solar projects involving multiple State departments and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the targets, if any, fixed for FSPV capacity addition by 2030?

(a) the State-wise and year-wise details of the total number and installed capacity of solar power plants, by category (ground-mounted, rooftop, agrivoltaics and others), during the last five years, including district-wise details for Andhra Pradesh;
(b) whether Government has conducted any study on the potential of agrivoltaics and other innovative solar deployment models to improve land-use efficiency, if so, the details and findings thereof; and
(c) whether any official definitions or standards have been developed or proposed for agrivoltaics and integrated solar systems, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether there is a specific push by Government to strengthen AYUSH infrastructure in Andhra Pradesh, including new colleges, hospitals and wellness centres;
(b) the central schemes, particularly the National AYUSH Mission (NAM), under which such support is being extended to the State;
(c) the broad funding pattern followed between the Centre and the State for such projects; and
(d) whether the Ministry reviews utilisation of funds released to States before sanctioning further support under the Mission?

(a) the current status of Inter-state Transmission System (ISTS) infrastructure required to evacuate solar power contracted by the State of Andhra Pradesh’s DISCOMs from the Solar Energy Corporation of India (SECI);
(b) the reasons, if any, for revision in the original supply timeline for this contracted power;
(c) the revised timeline envisaged for completion of the requisite transmission infrastructure; and
(d) the steps being taken by Government to expedite the augmentation of ISTS capacity to ensure timely evacuation of solar power for the State of Andhra Pradesh?

(a) whether the newly launched PMEGP 2.0 portal has achieved full API data integration with the Jan Samarth portal to enable real-time bank loan disbursements and the number of PMEGP applications from Andhra Pradesh processed through this integration so far;
(b) the number of rural micro-enterprises integrated into the Open Network for Digital Commerce ecosystem via the new MSME Global Mart 2.0 platform; and
(c) the timeline for completing the end-to-end digitisation of testing center activities under the newly functional national MSME Testing Portal and whether the MSME Technology Centre in Andhra Pradesh has been brought onto this testing platform?

(a) whether the newly integrated SNA-SPARSH funding module has eliminated delays in fund transfers to urban housing beneficiaries;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) the status of the State of Andhra Pradesh’s onboarding onto SNA-SPARSH and the number of houses sanctioned/completed in the State under PMAY-U 2.0 to date; and
(d) the steps taken under the Technology and Innovation Sub-Mission to promote green building standards in upcoming State partnership projects, including whether any Affordable Housing in Partnership (AHP) or Demonstration Housing Projects incorporating green building/modern construction technology have been approved for Andhra Pradesh?

(a) the current status of coordination between the Central Government and Government of Andhra Pradesh in identifying suitable sites, including along State and National Highways, for setting up public Electric Vehicle charging stations under schemes like PM e-DRIVE and FAME;
(b) whether the Ministry proposes any single-window clearance mechanism, State-Centre coordination platform, or dedicated nodal support to help Andhra Pradesh accelerate deployment of fast chargers under central schemes; and
(c) the steps being taken, or envisaged, to strengthen coordination with DISCOMs in Andhra Pradesh for grid preparedness to support the anticipated growth in electric vehicle charging demand in the State?

(a) the current status of implementation of the PLI scheme for automobile and auto components, and
the number of approved OEM/component companies with manufacturing units in Andhra Pradesh;
(b) the investment, production, and employment generated under the Scheme as of May 2026, with
State-wise/Andhra Pradesh-specific figures;
(c) whether the scheme has aided localisation of advanced automotive technologies/components in
Andhra Pradesh;
(d) the  progress achieved, including EV/component manufacturing progress in Andhra Pradesh, sector-wise; and
(e) if so, the details thereof, including any proposals to expand PLI-linked investment in the State?

(a) the objectives of Experiential Learning Programmes offered through MY Bharat platform and the manner in which these bridge the gap between academic learning and practical, real-world experience;
(b) the details of various such Programmes presently available on the platform across Government departments, educational institutions and businesses;
(c) the scale of participation in these programmes, including the number of youth who have enrolled in and completed Experiential Learning opportunities, State/UT-wise; and
(d) the broad framework of Experiential Learning model, including duration, structure and the role of MY Bharat NSS Programme Officers and Placement Officers in verification?

(a) the current status of Red Sanders smuggling in the country, particularly in Andhra Pradesh and whether the State has shown improved performance in curbing such smuggling in recent years;
(b) the details of Central assistance, including CAMPA funds, being extended to the State for protection of Red Sanders and conservation of its natural forests; and
(c) whether the Ministry proposes to strengthen inter-State coordination, satellite-based surveillance and CITES-related monitoring mechanisms to further support the State’s anti-smuggling efforts?

(a) the district-wise target for survey and physical registration of ancient scripts under the newly structured Gyan Bharatam Mission framework;
(b) whether the Ministry has integrated advanced Optical Character Recognition (OCR) technology on its portal to process the 18 crore newly digitised manuscript pages, and;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) how the Ministry plans to resolve copy-ownership and intellectual property challenges while allowing open public research access to rare religious manuscripts?

(a) the framework evolved for dissemination of geo-targeted emergency alerts through the indigenous Cell Broadcast System (CBS);
(b) whether the Ministry has completed the pan-India testing of the Cell Broadcasting System; 
(c) if so, the outcomes thereof; and
(d) the details of initiatives undertaken to improve coordination among telecom service providers and disaster management agencies for timely dissemination of emergency alerts?

(a) the current status of development of mega seafood processing parks and Aqua Parks across the country, and whether any such parks have been sanctioned or are under active consideration for Andhra Pradesh;
(b) the pattern of funding support extended by Government for these projects, including the share between the Centre and the States;
(c) the steps being taken by Government to boost processing capacity, branding and export-oriented manufacturing in the aquaculture sector; and
(d) whether Government proposes to undertake skill development and capacity-building initiatives for fish farmers, processing-unit workers and exporters?

(a) whether Government is aware of the growing adoption of nano urea and nano urea plus technology across the country and if so, the details of a policy framework and incentive structure to encourage domestic manufacturing and farmer-level uptake of nano-fertilizers;
(b) the details of nano urea farmer field trials and awareness-campaign in districts covering Andhra Pradesh; 
(c) whether any Central financial support has been extended to nano-fertilizer and specialty chemical units set up in Andhra Pradesh in the last two years, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) whether Government proposes to expand demonstration campaigns to more districts of Andhra Pradesh?

(a) the major seminars, conferences and outreach programmes organised by the National Commission for Minorities during 2026; 
(b) the key research studies commissioned or completed by the Commission during the said period and their objectives; 
(c) whether the findings and recommendations of such studies have been considered for policy formulation or implementation of minority welfare programmes;  
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the measures taken to strengthen engagement with State Minorities Commissions and minority communities through institutional outreach initiatives?

(a) details regarding the measures undertaken by Government to enhance mechanisation and strengthening of infrastructure in the coal sector, including adoption of advanced mining technologies, automation, conveyor systems and evacuation infrastructure;
(b) details regarding the projects proposed, under consideration and presently under implementation for mechanisation and infrastructure upgradation in coal mining across the country, State/UT-wise and in the State of Andhra Pradesh; and
(c) details regarding the scheme-wise and project-wise funds allocated, sanctioned, released and utilised for enhanced mechanisation and infrastructure development in the coal sector during the last five years, State/UT-wise and in the State of Andhra Pradesh?

(a) the details of the quantity and value of steel imported into the country during the last five years, including current year, category-wise, year-wise and country-wise;
(b) the quantity and value of steel exported from the country during the last five years including current year, year-wise, category-wise and destination-wise;
(c) the steel trade balance and the reasons for major changes in imports/exports, year-wise;
(d) whether Government has undertaken any measures to reduce import dependence and promote value-added steel exports, if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the details regarding the anti-dumping measures, quality control interventions implemented to regulate steel imports during the last five years?

(a) total length of rural roads constructed and number of habitations connected under various phases of the Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY) during financial year 2025-26;
(b) the plan for implementation of PMGSY during financial year 2026–27, particularly regarding upgradation and maintenance of roads, if any;
(c) the targets set for construction and upgradation of rural roads under the scheme, State-wise;
(d) whether any mechanism has been adopted to prioritize road connectivity in aspirational districts, tribal and remote regions, if so, details thereof; and
(e) the proposed investment for implementation of the scheme, including respective contributions of Centre and States, the details thereof?

(a) the progress made in the deployment of Kavach 4.0m, including the route kilometres and locomotives covered as of date;
(b) the railway zones and high-density corridors identified for implementation during 2026-27, State & district-wise including Uttar Pradesh;
(c) whether any timeline has been prescribed for network-wise deployment of Kavach, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the measures taken to accelerate the installation and commissioning of Kavach across the Indian Railways network?

(a) the details regarding the incentives and support mechanisms in place by Government for development of One District One Product (ODOP) industries, including financial assistance, credit support, skill development, common facility centres, quality certification, branding and marketing support;
(b) the details of convergence of ODOP with other Central schemes such as MSME, PMFME, Skill India and export promotion programmes;
(c) the details of mechanisms adopted to facilitate market access for ODOP products, including e-commerce integration, domestic and international exhibitions, buyer–seller meets and export facilitation; and
(d) the details of outcomes of these initiatives including employment generation and exports under ODOP during the last five years, State/UT-wise?

(a) whether Government has achieved the target of distributing 15000 drones to Women Self Help Groups (SHGs) under Namo Drone Didi scheme for years 2023-24 to 2025-26;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) if not, the reasons therefor along with steps taken to accelerate distribution of the remaining drones and timelines;
(d) the total number of drones sanctioned/ allocated and distributed since inception, State-wise and district-wise for Andhra Pradesh;
(e) the details regarding the criteria used for allocation of drones to States; and
(f) the details regarding the list of Lead Fertilizer Companies (LFCs) responsible for implementation of the scheme in Andhra Pradesh?

(a) the steps taken by Government to reduce the number of fake immigration agents during the last five years, State-wise especially from Andhra Pradesh;
(b) the number of fake immigration agents identified, arrested, under trial and convicted during that period, State-wise including Andhra Pradesh; and
(c) whether Government has undertaken any campaigns to inform and educate citizens regarding the issue of fake immigration agents and if so, the details regarding such exercises undertaken across the country during those years, State-wise including Andhra Pradesh?

(a) the details of training centres/institutes in nuclear technology functioning at present, including location, courses offered and training capacity, institute-wise;
(b) the details of skill development and workforce training programmes conducted for technicians, engineers and skilled manpower in nuclear energy and allied sectors during the last five years, year-wise;
(c) the details regarding the number of trainees trained, certified and absorbed in nuclear facilities and related industries during that period, institute-wise; and 
(d) whether Government has taken any steps to strengthen the skill development ecosystem in nuclear technology and if so, the details thereof?
